WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.135
- Because we're so
close to the border,

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.870
I want to add some
Text Mex flavors

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.606
to my menu at the final cook.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.742
I'm about to meet an
expert who still makes

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.978
the traditional corn tortillas
today, which may just

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.047
give me that edge over Justin.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:14.981
Emmanuel.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:15.815
- Morning.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:16.683
How you doing?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.250
- Very well, thanks.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:17.884
But how are you?

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:18.718
- Great.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.486
Welcome to Texas.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.320
- Oh, my Lord.

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.020
Good to see you, [inaudible].

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.155
- You too.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.323
- Emmanuel Chavez
is a local chef

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.357
whose life is fueled
by his passion

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.825
for the traditional tortilla.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.726
- Super Important.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.994
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.496
You can't come to
Texas and not represent

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.764
the other side of the border.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.831
And I'm going to show
you how to do it.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.866
- Please.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.833
- We're gonna do it together.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.435
- Please, please, please.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.004
Emanuel starts with a lesson on
how to make the perfect masa,

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.907
a dough made from corn.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.442
- So right here we have conico.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.210
It's a native seed from Mexico.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.745
This is our base
for our tortilla,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.713
- Got you.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.647
- And it turns into masa.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.548
- So the idea now
is to grind it?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.182
- Correct.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.049
- So it's a blue.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:50.884
- It is a blue corn.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.518
And it stays blue.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:52.085
- Wow.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.253
- It's gorgeous.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.020
We're going to make
blue tortillas.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.654
Should we start?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.588
- Yes.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.823
You're going to
grab a little bit

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.524
of a handful of these conico.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.558
- Got you.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.459
- You're going to
start from the top.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.493
- Got you.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.060
- You to do almost
like a pasta motion.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:01.694
- Right.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.096
So.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:03.997
- With your wrist, you're
going to roll forward

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:04.864
and then roll backwards.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:05.965
There you go.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.866
There you go.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.801
- Oh my God.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.235
Wow.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.705
They're incredibly
powdery, now isn't it?

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.973
That's the masa coming out.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:14.908
- That's the starch.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.342
- The starch.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.744
- You're doing great.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.479
- The challenge for
me was the grinding.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.649
So you're sort of rolling,
spinning, rolling, spinning.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.650
It's all in the wrist.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.251
Man, that's incredible.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.320
- Grab a little bit and
just make it into a ball,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.621
a nice little ball.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.623
- It looks dry, but
it's actually quite wet.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.257
Yeah.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.158
No, it's perfect.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.026
It's the perfect masa.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.627
You did a great job.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.997
- Masa made, and with Emmanuel's
brisket already simmering,

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.699
I'm dying to make a tortilla.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.067
But we're not done.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.770
- Before we finish our tacos,
we need one more ingredient.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:44.771
- One more ingredient?

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:45.505
- I show you where it's at.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.272
- Seriously?

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.807
- The [inaudible] pepper.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:48.942
- [inaudible] pepper.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.410
- The national
pepper from Texas.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.411
- Wow.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:56.916
Bloody hell.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:57.917
Are they uh--

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.852
- Longhorns.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.752
Texas longhorns.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.386
- Absolutely.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:00.954
Yeah.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.588
- Oh my goodness.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.155
- Yeah.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.122
Gorgeous, huh?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.124
- Man, they are peaceful.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.960
Look at those.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.661
How majestic are they?

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.330
- They're big boys, too.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.030
- OK.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:11.998
Let's not get them mad.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:12.932
[inaudible] but.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:13.833
- Let's go.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.268
OK.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.569
- Where are those peppers?

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.770
- They're right
there in that corner.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.671
- That's them there?

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.506
- That's it right here.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.207
They're gorgeous, aren't they?

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.575
- That's incredible how they
just grow wild like that.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.309
Huh?

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.210
So red and green.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.211
- Red and green, yeah.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.346
- Red's super hot, right?

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:27.480
- Yeah.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.548
I'm going to try a green
one, just to be safe.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:31.518
Go from there.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.919
Yeah.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.053
- Oh!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.054
Man.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.456
- That's Texas right there.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.790
- So the idea is to
lightly press them and then

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.791
finish them in the stew?

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.826
- Absolutely.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.460
That's what we're going to do.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.127
- Man.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.395
Excellent.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.900
- All of them in there?

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.234
- Yeah.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.270
- Peppers crushed and
added to the brisket.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:53.306
It's time to finish
making the tortillas.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.541
- That should be fine.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:54.974
Yeah.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:55.608
- There?

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.242
- Yeah.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.477
That's beautiful.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.511
Actually, you don't
have to rotate it.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.178
It's perfect.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.812
- Nah, look at that.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.613
- Yeah.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.047
You've [inaudible].

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.181
- Wow.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:02.882
That's straight
into the skillet?

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.017
- Yeah.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:04.884
And you're going
to do one motion.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.652
Don't toss it.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.452
Just gently--

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:06.953
- Gently.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.854
- Love it.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.922
Make love to it.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.323
There you go.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.157
- Wow.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.458
The color of those things.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.193
As soon as you see the
edges start to cook

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.094
a little bit, like that one--

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.029
- Yes.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.163
- --I'd give it a flip.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:17.897
- Just flip it
with your fingers?

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.798
- Yeah.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.100
Just ready to flip.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.402
- Tortillas finished.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.737
It's time to taste the
fruits of our labor.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.544
[bleep]

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.612
- Oh, my God.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.480
That is incredible.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.315
Wow.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:36.616
What a delicious combination.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.718
But it starts with the
base, the foundation

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.019
of the Tex-Mex tortilla.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.354
Nothing is disintegrating.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.022
I was slightly nervous
about how thin it was.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.557
It's so pliable.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.160
And the starchiness is absorbing
all that incredible flavor

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.661
from the brisket.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.698
- Getting to grips with a
authentic tortilla, for me,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:55.168
makes that dish transform into
something even more delicious.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.203
I'd love to use these for
the one I'm gonna cook.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.037
- Absolutely.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:58.871
- Would you mind?

00:03:58.938 --> 00:03:59.639
- No, not at all.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.173
- You're a star.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:00.873
- Thank you.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.608
- Thanks, bud.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.175
- Good luck.

